WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.580
A two-pack of Epipens costs over $600 for an old, inexpensive drug. This is First Principles

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:11.640
Daily, episode 172. The device delivers a measured dose of epinephrine through a spring-driven

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:18.180
needle in a single-use plastic housing. That two-pack list price sat near $100 in 2007

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:23.880
and had climbed past 600 by the middle of the 2010s, though the active ingredient has been

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:29.200
synthesized since the early 20th century. The spread between a commodity drug and the finished

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.840
device is the engineering, the regulation, and the market sitting on the materials.

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:39.360
For someone in anaphylaxis, the injector has to fire after years in a pocket or a purse.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:43.500
Get through clothing and reach muscle when fine motor control is gone.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:49.080
The price path asks how much of the bill is those requirements, and how much is protection

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:50.320
piled on the mechanism.

00:00:51.345 --> 00:00:57.405
The spring-loaded injector began as military hardware in the 1950s and 1960s, built to deliver

00:00:57.405 --> 00:01:03.405
nerve-agent antidotes. Engineer Sheldon Kaplan, working at survival technology, adapted

00:01:03.405 --> 00:01:08.925
the spring-loaded glass cartridge design for civilian use in the 1970s. The Food and Drug

00:01:08.925 --> 00:01:15.405
Administration approved the Epipen in December 1987. Meridian medical technologies later acquired

00:01:15.405 --> 00:01:21.585
by King Pharmaceuticals, and then tied to Milen, has manufactured the units under contract for decades.

00:01:21.585 --> 00:01:27.525
rates. Repeated device patents carried protection out to 2025. The Food and Drug Administration

00:01:27.525 --> 00:01:33.425
treats different auto-injector designs as non-interchangeable, so a pharmacy cannot substitute one

00:01:33.425 --> 00:01:38.965
for another on its own. Schools and emergency protocols often specify the branded two-pack,

00:01:39.445 --> 00:01:45.465
which keeps demand on the higher-priced version. Milen took the marketing rights in 2007, when

00:01:45.465 --> 00:01:50.965
annual sales sat near $200 million. By the middle of the following decade, sales exceeded

00:01:50.965 --> 00:01:52.465
did $1 billion a year.

00:01:53.005 --> 00:01:55.365
List prices for competing auto-injectors,

00:01:55.725 --> 00:01:56.925
Adrenalic click among them,

00:01:57.205 --> 00:01:58.865
rose sharply over the same years.

00:01:59.505 --> 00:02:01.125
Drug patents had already expired.

00:02:01.705 --> 00:02:03.185
What held the old price structure

00:02:03.185 --> 00:02:05.085
was patent-protected device features,

00:02:05.545 --> 00:02:07.165
those non-equivalence rulings

00:02:07.165 --> 00:02:09.925
and prescribing habits concentrated on one product.

00:02:10.525 --> 00:02:12.325
A new manufacturer still has to clear

00:02:12.325 --> 00:02:14.645
the same device-specific regulatory bar,

00:02:15.105 --> 00:02:17.005
even if the drug substance is identical,

00:02:17.585 --> 00:02:20.025
and prescribers and institutions keep defaulting

00:02:20.025 --> 00:02:21.765
to the product they already train on.

00:02:22.205 --> 00:02:26.385
The spring, the needle, the glass cartridge, and the plastic shell stay inexpensive.

00:02:27.225 --> 00:02:29.745
The assembled and approved product keeps the premium.

00:02:30.838 --> 00:02:35.118
The research sources for this episode do not contain the material quantities or commodity

00:02:35.118 --> 00:02:40.218
prices needed to price the housing, the spring, the needle, and the glass cartridge as raw

00:02:40.218 --> 00:02:40.858
stuff alone.

00:02:41.438 --> 00:02:46.238
Without those figures there is no magic wand number, and a first principles ratio cannot

00:02:46.238 --> 00:02:47.918
be constructed from the given data.

00:02:48.378 --> 00:02:49.598
I will not invent one.

00:02:49.598 --> 00:02:55.178
What the record does show as the heavy cost is regulatory exclusivity on the device mechanism.

00:02:55.458 --> 00:02:59.778
The manufacturing and quality systems required for an emergency use product

00:02:59.778 --> 00:03:05.198
and the distribution arrangements that tie the injector to specific prescribing and stocking rules.

00:03:05.698 --> 00:03:09.358
Those layers sit between the epinephrine solution and the packaged price.

00:03:10.118 --> 00:03:16.758
Generic entrants that reached the market after 2025 have listed two packs between $175 and $300,

00:03:16.758 --> 00:03:21.778
dollars, which shows that some of the earlier premium was tied to exclusivity rather than

00:03:21.778 --> 00:03:23.418
to material or assembly cost.

00:03:24.178 --> 00:03:29.098
A nasal spray alternative approved in 2024 separates the delivery step from the legacy

00:03:29.098 --> 00:03:30.098
mechanical design.

00:03:30.778 --> 00:03:35.038
The distance left between the lowest of those generic two packs and the branded product

00:03:35.038 --> 00:03:39.958
is the share of the old list price held up by patent extensions and the non-interchange

00:03:39.958 --> 00:03:44.298
ability determinations, not by fabricating the spring or filling the cartridge.

00:03:44.298 --> 00:03:48.778
average. The spray removes the needle and the spring and replaces them with a propellant

00:03:48.778 --> 00:03:54.458
driven mist. That path still required four dedicated pharmacokinetic studies, and the

00:03:54.458 --> 00:03:59.318
finished form bypasses the mechanical assembly that had anchored the prior exclusivity window.

00:04:00.384 --> 00:04:05.824
ARS Pharmaceuticals developed Neffi, the first epinephrine nasal spray the Food and Drug Administration

00:04:05.824 --> 00:04:11.824
approved. After four clinical studies in 175 adults showed blood levels comparable to

00:04:11.824 --> 00:04:17.524
injected products. The August 2024 approval covers patients weighing at least 30 kilograms

00:04:17.944 --> 00:04:23.604
and takes the needle out entirely. Generic auto-injectors from TIVA and AMNEL and authorized

00:04:23.604 --> 00:04:30.644
generic sold by Beatrice now compete at lower-list prices. A from scratch redesign could first go after

00:04:30.644 --> 00:04:36.004
the spring and cartridge assembly and ask whether additive manufacturing or standardized commodity

00:04:36.004 --> 00:04:41.144
components could cut the part count while keeping the force profile needed for reliable intramuscular

00:04:41.144 --> 00:04:45.824
delivery under panic. Second, it could ask whether pathways for device drug

00:04:45.824 --> 00:04:50.784
combinations can be shortened, once bioequivalence data exists, so a device

00:04:50.784 --> 00:04:54.644
improvement does not stretch an exclusivity window the way the earlier patents

00:04:54.644 --> 00:04:59.264
did. Third, it could test whether stocking policies and school mandates can

00:04:59.264 --> 00:05:04.604
accept any approved delivery format rather than one branded mechanism. Each step

00:05:04.604 --> 00:05:08.904
still needs demonstrated reliability in real anaphylaxis and acceptance from

00:05:08.904 --> 00:05:11.864
prescribers who have trained on the legacy device for years.

00:05:12.504 --> 00:05:17.484
The spray already shows that the core requirement, rapid systemic epinephrine at the right dose,

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:22.604
can be met without that mechanical assembly, provided the other route produces matching

00:05:22.604 --> 00:05:25.184
blood concentrations and hemodynamic effects.

00:05:25.904 --> 00:05:30.804
Any further cost cut would still have to clear the same safety threshold that originally justified

00:05:30.804 --> 00:05:36.044
the device patterns, which is why what remains after generic entry is the cost of keeping

00:05:36.044 --> 00:05:39.424
that verified performance, not the raw materials alone.

00:05:40.144 --> 00:05:44.644
A price shaped more by exclusivity and by prescribing convention than by the physical

00:05:44.644 --> 00:05:49.284
parts leaves room for any new delivery format that meets the same safety threshold.

00:05:49.964 --> 00:05:53.844
The open question is whether evidence can travel from one format to another.

00:05:54.484 --> 00:05:59.164
Who will next publish head-to-head data that lets pharmacists substitute across formats without

00:05:59.164 --> 00:05:59.944
new legislation?

